# Copy this file to backend/.env and fill in what you have.
#
#   cp backend/.env.example backend/.env
#
# backend/.env is gitignored. Never commit a real key: this repository will be
# shared, and a key committed once stays in the git history even after it is
# deleted from the file.
#
# Everything here is optional. With none of it set, the backend runs on
# deterministic rules and an in-memory store, and says so on /api/v1/health.

# --- Gemini -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Get a key from https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#
# The key ALONE is not enough — the SDK has to be installed too:
#     .venv/bin/pip install google-genai
# Without it the backend stays on rules and /api/v1/health will tell you so.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional. Defaults to gemini-3.8-flash.
#
# gemini-2.5-flash is retired for new keys: models.list() still shows it, but
# using it returns 404. If the default is busy (503 UNAVAILABLE / 504, which
# happens — flagship models spike), switch to a lighter one and the demo
# keeps its Gemini reasoning:
#
#     GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.1-flash-lite
#
# The backend falls back to rules on any model failure, so a 503 degrades the
# reasoning rather than breaking the demo — but you lose the Gemini story,
# which is usually the point.
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.8-flash

# --- Firestore (optional persistence) ---------------------------------------
# Without this the store is in-memory and state is lost on restart — which on
# Cloud Run happens whenever it scales to zero.
#     .venv/bin/pip install google-cloud-firestore
#     gcloud auth application-default login
#     gcloud firestore databases create --location=asia-south1
# FIRESTORE_PROJECT=gen-lang-client-0373165899
#
# If Google APIs reject calls with "User project specified in the request is
# invalid", the application-default credentials carry a stale quota project:
#     gcloud auth application-default set-quota-project gen-lang-client-0373165899

# To develop against the emulator instead of real Firestore (free, local,
# and wiped when you stop it):
#     JAVA_HOME=/opt/homebrew/opt/openjdk@24 \
#       gcloud emulators firestore start --host-port=127.0.0.1:8900 --quiet
#     FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST=127.0.0.1:8900
# FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST=127.0.0.1:8900

# --- Cloud Storage (optional durable media) ---------------------------------
# Without this, photos and voice clips go to local disk. On Cloud Run that
# disk is per-instance and discarded on restart, so the incident record
# outlives the evidence it points at. /api/v1/health reports which it is.
#     .venv/bin/pip install google-cloud-storage
#     gcloud storage buckets create gs://avertis-media-<something-unique> \
#       --location=asia-south1 --uniform-bucket-level-access
#
# This bucket already exists and is verified working:
# STORAGE_BUCKET=avertis-media-0373165899

# --- Shared key between the mesh and this backend (optional) ----------------
# If set, callers must send it as the X-Avertis-Key header. Leave empty for
# local development.
# AVERTIS_API_KEY=
